{"hash": "6b7b97953a439908", "text": "Every house has suppliers. In code, they're dependencies: other people's libraries your program pulls in. Even when everyone on the team codes with AI, someone who knows the libraries should decide which ones the program uses. Otherwise AI keeps adding more, a new package for every want. Each one is a stranger's code, running with your keys. One study this year found agents' package choices made security worse on balance, where people's made it better. AI still sometimes names packages that don't exist, and attackers register the names it tends to invent. Self-spreading worms have hit the JavaScript package registry again and again since last September; this August's also hid files in a hijacked project's own code, set to run the moment someone opened it in an AI editor. You'll meet it as five new lines in your package list that nobody asked for.", "alignment": {"characters": ["E", "v", "e", "r", "y", " ", "h", "o", "u", "s", "e", " ", "h", "a", "s", " ", "s", "u", "p", "p", "l", "i", "e", "r", "s", ".", " ", "I", "n", " ", "c", "o", "d", "e", ",", " ", "t", "h", "e", "y", "'", "r", "e", " ", "d", "e", "p", "e", "n", "d", "e", "n", "c", "i", "e", "s", ":", " ", "o", "t", "h", "e", "r", " ", "p", "e", "o", "p", "l", "e", "'", "s", " ", "l", "i", "b", "r", "a", "r", "i", "e", "s", " ", "y", "o", "u", "r", " ", "p", "r", "o", "g", "r", "a", "m", " ", "p", "u", "l", "l", "s", " ", "i", "n", ".", " ", "E", "v", "e", "n", " ", "w", "h", "e", "n", " ", "e", "v", "e", "r", "y", "o", "n", "e", " ", "o", "n", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "t", "e", "a", "m", " ", "c", "o", "d", "e", "s", " ", "w", "i", "t", "h", " ", "A", "I", ",", " ", "s", "o", "m", "e", "o", "n", "e", " ", "w", "h", "o", " ", "k", "n", "o", "w", "s", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "l", "i", "b", "r", "a", "r", "i", "e", "s", " ", "s", "h", "o", "u", "l", "d", " ", "d", "e", "c", "i", "d", "e", " ", "w", "h", "i", "c", "h", " ", "o", "n", "e", "s", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "p", "r